# Aitosoft: what `az acr build` must not upload.
#
# The build context is the developer's working tree, and the Dockerfile does
# `COPY . /tmp/project/`. Until 2026-11-03 there was no .dockerignore, and the
# production image 0.9.2-capacity-gate-2 was found to contain /tmp/project/.env
# (the API token), .env.txt, PRIVATE.md, tmp/ (cross-repo messages) and
# test-aitosoft/artifacts/ (stored customer captures). The registry is private,
# so the readers were the same Azure principals who can read the Container App's
# env vars; it is still nothing an image needs. Gitignored local state belongs
# here too. Keep the build inputs (crawl4ai/, deploy/, pyproject.toml, setup.py,
# azure-deployment/pip-constraints.txt, ...) out of this list.

# secrets and private identifiers
.env
.env.*
PRIVATE.md

# local evidence, messages and customer data
tmp/
test-aitosoft/artifacts/
dump.rdb
*.rdb

# local tooling state
.git/
.claude/
.context/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
